implementationPlan.description:
postflight.sh scenarios (scripts/tests/postflight.sh).

Build on the landed WT-04/05/06 worktree fixture: a scratch project whose fake claim carries workspace mode worktree, with W = .worktrees/<taskId> on moe/task/<taskId> and the control on moe/control. If a helper is missing, add one small `make_wt_project` beside make_scope_project.

Add scenarios WT7A-WT7F. Bump the counter guard (scope_expected_runs and the name list in its message) by the number added. Leave every existing scenario untouched (DoD 5). Use scope_fail, run_scope_wrapper, committed_paths and node checks over record_commit.jsonl / evidence-rpcs.jsonl.

- WT7A (DoD 1): the fake CLI edits a tracked file and adds a new one in W; exit WORKING. Assert:
  - moe/task/<id> gains exactly one commit, whose first parent is the previous tip and whose tree has both files;
  - the target sha, the control HEAD and sha, its index (`diff --cached --quiet`) and its `status --porcelain` output are unchanged;
  - the last record_commit row matches {outcome:'committed', kind:'checkpoint', ref:'refs/heads/moe/task/<id>', paths:[both, sorted], inferredPaths:[], unattributedPaths:[]} via deepStrictEqual on those keys;
  - nothing was pushed (no remote).
- WT7B (DoD 2): the CLI also writes W/.mcp.json, W/.codex/x, W/.claude/skills/s.md (the link path WT-06 makes, as a plain dir here) and an untracked W/.serena/f. Assert MOE_ATTR_EXCLUDED is in the output, none of those paths is in the commit tree, and no baseline file exists under the control gitdir or W's gitdir.
- WT7C (DoD 3, recovery): leave W dirty from a first run (MOE_DISABLE_CHECKPOINT=1), then make a normal run. Assert:
  - MOE_CHECKPOINT_RECOVERED task=<id> sha=<sha>;
  - that wip subject ends ' recovered' and its tree holds the leftover file;
  - it is the parent of the session's own checkpoint.
  Negative (spike comment-40613e9a): leftover dirt plus W/.moe/x gives no new commit on moe/task/<id>, and the dirt and W/.moe/x stay intact.
- WT7D (DoD 3, control seats): with the control on moe/control, an architect run and a QA run whose CLI writes a file in the control. Each:
  - prints MOE_COMMIT_NOTHING_TO_COMMIT and records outcome nothing with that code;
  - leaves `git for-each-ref` output equal before and after (no commit on any ref);
  - keeps HEAD on refs/heads/moe/control and writes no baseline.
- WT7E (DoD 4): <control>/pre.txt is dirty before the run, and the worker CLI writes <control>/stray.txt by absolute path. Assert:
  - MOE_WORKTREE_STRAY_EDIT is printed;
  - exactly one add_comment row in .moe/evidence-rpcs.jsonl names stray.txt and not pre.txt;
  - stray.txt keeps its bytes, and `git log --all --format=%H -- stray.txt` is empty.
- WT7F (push): with checkpointPush on and a local bare remote, the task branch is pushed and the remote sha equals the local tip. Then pre-seed the remote's moe/task/<id> with a divergent commit: the output carries CHECKPOINT-UNPUSHED, and the local and remote refs are unchanged (no force).

Keep fixtures small; each scenario proves one behavior.
